    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, but doesn't that come at a cost though? It feels like some of the most famous contemporary pieces today are basically just propaganda or manifestos, and they lack any real craft or visual appeal. Don't you think the focus on \"discursive power\" has actually led to a decline in the actual quality and artistry of what's being produced?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While some certainly perceive a dilution of craft, this critique often overlooks the evolving definition of \"artistry\" itself. In postmodernism, the concept of the handmade object has often been intentionally undermined to prioritize the idea over flawless execution. The \"craft\" is sometimes relocated from the visible finish to the intellectual complexity or the political insight embedded in the concept. Therefore, the perceived lack of beauty is often itself a deliberate aesthetic strategy designed to challenge bourgeois notions of taste.",
      "source": "target",
